t does not end in a precise research question or hypothesis. Add an explicit question such as whether a low-cost differential-drive, 3D-printed platform can satisfy a defined subset of SS\L performance constraints under a specified control architecture. Or Consider focusing on performance in particular scenarios. It is ok if we deviate from these scenarios later but we need to have one in mind here.</span></p></body>)/Rect[192.734 621.484 216.734 645.484]/Subj(Sticky Note)/Subtype/Text/T(brand)/Type/Annot>>endobj5 0 obj<</F 28/Open true/Page 4/Parent 4 0 R/Rect[112.925 657.949 296.866 841.89]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj6 0 obj<</C[0.858826 0.203918 0.145096]/Contents(You introduce PID and MPC, but the methodology later implements only PID. Remove MPC from the framing unless the proposal will genuinely compare controllers.)/CreationDate(D:20260531175429+02'00')/F 28/M(D:20260531175443+02'00')/NM(8415745c-fb2a-4089-a931-48ae7a8125e7)/Name/Comment/Page 6/Popup 7 0 R/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:26.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;\font-style:normal">You introduce PID and MPC, but the methodology later implements only PID. Remove MPC from the framing unless the proposal will genuinely compare controllers.</span></p></body>)/Rect[56.8567 84.4011 80.8567 108.401]/Subj(Sticky Note)/Subtype/Text/T(brand)/Type/Annot>>endobj7 0 obj<</F 28/Open true/Page 6/Parent 6 0 R/Rect[594.922 28.2365 778.863 156.995]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj8 0 obj<</C[0.858826 0.203918 0.145096]/Contents(The literature review does not distinguish clearly between educational low-cost platforms and competition-grade SSL robots. Build that distinction explicitly because it is central to the proposed contribution.)/CreationDate(D:20260531175809+02'00')/F 28/M(D:20260531175812+02'00')/NM(dca06851-8d14-47e0-91c1-568c16171815)/Name/Comment/Page 8/Popup 9 0 R/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:26.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;\font-style:normal">The literature review does not distinguish clearly between educational low-cost platforms and competition-grade SSL robots. Build that distinction explicitly because it is central to the proposed contribution.</span></p></body>)/Rect[51.3482 491.115 75.3482 515.115]/Subj(Sticky Note)/Subtype/Text/T(brand)/Type/Annot>>endobj9 0 obj<</F 28/Open true/Page 8/Parent 8 0 R/Rect[594.922 375.255 778.863 515.05]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj10 0 obj<</C[0.858826 0.203918 0.145096]/Contents(We need a problem statement and research questions section with appropriate content included.\r\rRight now the proposal says, in effect, "I will build a robot and test it." That is not enough for research. The reader needs to know exactly what you are try\ing to prove. Otherwise, even if the robot works, it will be unclear what lesson the results are meant to support.\r\rState one primary research question and, if needed, one or two secondary questions. For example: can a low-cost differential-drive platfo\rm built from 3D-printed parts and low-cost electronics satisfy a defined subset of SSL motion and control requirements? Then map each benchmark directly to that question.)/CreationDate(D:20260531181018+02'00')/F 28/M(D:20260531181127+02'00')/NM(62a16841-0486-4745-a3ea-f82d993b6a37)/Name/Comment/Page 11/Popup 11 0 R/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:26.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;\font-style:normal">We need a problem statement and research questions section with appropriate content included.&#13;&#13;Right now the proposal says, in effect, &quot;I will build a robot and test it.&quot; That is not enough for research. The reader nee\ds to know exactly what you are trying to prove. Otherwise, even if the robot works, it will be unclear what lesson the results are meant to support.&#13;&#13;State one primary research question and, if needed, one or two secondary questions. For example:\ can a low-cost differential-drive platform built from 3D-printed parts and low-cost electronics satisfy a defined subset of SSL motion and control requirements? Then map each benchmark directly to that question.</span></p></body>)/Rect[311.168 643.518 335.168 667.518]/Subj(Sticky Note)/Subtype/Text/T(brand)/Type/Annot>>endobj11 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Page 11/Parent 10 0 R/Rect[594.922 490.344 778.863 667.453]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj12 0 obj<</C[0.858826 0.203918 0.145096]/CA 0.399994/Contents(The controller is framed as a wheel-velocity controller, but the measured feedback signal is an MPU6050 accelerometer.\r\rIs that not misaligned, or am I confused, are you trying to control speed using a sensor that does not directly tell you the speed yo\u need.)/CreationDate(D:20260531181248+02'00')/F 4/IT/HighlightNote/M(D:20260531181352+02'00')/NM(c0294cce-cc11-4a41-84cc-039b503dd016)/Page 12/Popup 13 0 R/QuadPoints[481.106 726.11 523.272 726.11 481.106 711.776 523.272 711.776 72.0 711.664 523.272 711.664 72.0 697.33 523.272 697.33 72.0 697.218 255.345 697.218 72.0 682.884 255.345 682.884]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:26.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;\font-style:normal">The controller is framed as a wheel-velocity controller, but the measured feedback signal is an MPU6050 accelerometer.&#13;&#13;Is that not misaligned, or am I confused, are you trying to control speed using a sensor that does not direc\tly tell you the speed you need.</span></p></body>)/Rect[71.552 682.436 523.72 726.558]/Subj(Comment on Text)/Subtype/Highlight/T(brand)/Type/Annot>>endobj13 0 obj<</F 28/Open true/Page 12/Parent 12 0 R/Rect[594.922 553.306 778.863 726.211]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj14 0 obj<</C[0.858826 0.203918 0.145096]/Contents(Can we restucture this\r\rTo have sections for different scenarios which are going to be used to benchmark the two robots.\r\rAnd inside each of these or seperately we have a section called metrics which formalise how we are going to score each of these.\r\\rYou kinda have the metrics just not the scenarios, these could be goto X tasks, which or other types of navigation as an example)/CreationDate(D:20260531180020+02'00')/F 28/M(D:20260531180337+02'00')/NM(4ca0296e-2485-4c98-ae55-d28a591402d8)/Name/Comment/Page 13/Popup 15 0 R/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:26.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;\font-style:normal">Can we restucture this&#13;&#13;To have sections for different scenarios which are going to be used to benchmark the two robots.&#13;&#13;And inside each of these or seperately we have a section called metrics which formalise how we are\ going to score each of these.&#13;&#13;You kinda have the metrics just not the scenarios, these could be goto X tasks, which or other types of navigation as an example</span></p></body>)/Rect[17.3789 278.118 41.3789 302.118]/Subj(Sticky Note)/Subtype/Text/T(brand)/Type/Annot>>endobj15 0 obj<</F 28/Open true/Page 13/Parent 14 0 R/Rect[594.922 118.112 778.863 302.053]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj16 0 obj<</C[0.858826 0.203918 0.145096]/CA 0.399994/Contents(ideally not have this overlap)/CreationDate(D:20260531180407+02'00')/