/Type/Annot>>endobj20 0 obj<</C[0.858826 0.203918 0.145096]/Contents(I know we have been going with the turtlebot, but we actually have Jetbots as well. For better science lets include a 3rd baseline that of the JetBot - https://jetbot.org/master/)/CreationDate(D:20260531181456+02'00')/F 28/M(D:20260531181607+02'00')/NM(080a1f15-62c2-45b7-bbc5-1ac8b3f26ce5)/Name/Comment/Page 13/Popup 21 0 R/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:26.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;\font-style:normal">I know we have been going with the turtlebot, but we actually have Jetbots as well. For better science lets include a 3rd baseline that of the JetBot - https://jetbot.org/master/</span></p></body>)/Rect[33.9045 46.7595 57.9045 70.7595]/Subj(Sticky Note)/Subtype/Text/T(brand)/Type/Annot>>endobj21 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Page 13/Parent 20 0 R/Rect[594.922 73.2229 778.863 201.981]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj22 0 obj<</C[0.858826 0.203918 0.145096]/Contents(The software stack is described in a way that mixes different generations of ROS. That makes it hard to know what system is actually being built, and the timing results depend on that choice. Can you maybe just let me know why the different versions are n\eeded like over WhatsApp)/CreationDate(D:20260531181642+02'00')/F 28/M(D:20260531181727+02'00')/NM(8959e1c9-0e09-43df-b453-f76a247c1363)/Name/Comment/Page 13/Popup 23 0 R/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:26.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;\font-style:normal">The software stack is described in a way that mixes different generations of ROS. That makes it hard to know what system is actually being built, and the timing results depend on that choice. Can you maybe just let me know why the diffe\rent versions are needed like over WhatsApp</span></p></body>)/Rect[400.222 677.487 424.222 701.487]/Subj(Sticky Note)/Subtype/Text/T(brand)/Type/Annot>>endobj23 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Page 13/Parent 22 0 R/Rect[594.922 550.591 778.863 701.422]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj24 0 obj<</C[0.858826 0.203918 0.145096]/CA 0.399994/Contents(The path-following test uses an M-shaped trajectory without explaining why that path is representative. Justify the path design or include several path classes that test straight motion, turning, and stop-start control separately.)/CreationDate(D:20260531180716+02'00')/F 4/IT/HighlightNote/M(D:20260531180729+02'00')/NM(a93ee458-ff75-488d-97b6-f8d64bc73955)/Page 14/Popup 25 0 R/QuadPoints[504.942 616.775 523.281 616.775 504.942 602.441 523.281 602.441 72.0 602.329 163.636 602.329 72.0 587.995 163.636 587.995]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:26.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;\font-style:normal">The path-following test uses an M-shaped trajectory without explaining why that path is representative. Justify the path design or include several path classes that test straight motion, turning, and stop-start control separately.</span\></p></body>)/Rect[71.5521 587.547 523.729 617.223]/Subj(Comment on Text)/Subtype/Highlight/T(brand)/Type/Annot>>endobj25 0 obj<</F 28/Open true/Page 14/Parent 24 0 R/Rect[594.922 477.163 778.863 616.958]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj26 0 obj<</C[0.858826 0.203918 0.145096]/CA 0.399994/Contents(This is very optimistic, what is the maximum time you are allowed.)/CreationDate(D:20260531180853+02'00')/F 4/IT/HighlightNote/M(D:20260531180913+02'00')/NM(ca8e9ea1-c637-4c29-ba6f-454d4aa0215c)/Page 16/Popup 27 0 R/QuadPoints[1